{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1093459-how-to-cheat-at-being-a-shapechanger","id":1093459,"title":"How to cheat at being a Shapechanger","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-16T17:02:57-07:00","id":1093459,"title":"How to cheat at being a Shapechanger","content":"First off, I am not looking for something overpowered or broken.<br /> <br /> For a game, one player was talking about making an Kinfolk that was unhappy that they didn't change. After the character Awoke they have been trying to use magic, wonders and anything else they can find to gain what they feel is their rightful abilities.<br /> <br /> While I know the easy answers of use Sphere X to do effect X, I am wondering if anyone has unique or interesting ideas for a mage to cheat at being a shapechanger of any kind. We are not looking to recreate Samuel Haight or get the full powers of being a were-whatever, but to find thematically interesting ways to move forward with this idea.<br /> <br /> Especially beneficial is any way of accomplishing any particular feat without the player needing Spheres; for example Forged by Dragons Fire has a wonder tattoo that allows one to shapechange into one particular animal and certain fetishes from Werewolf could help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8764-zulkir-jhor","name":"Zulkir Jhor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T19:28:51-07:00","id":1093496,"title":"","content":"Well there is always the infernal route, granted you might gain some taint and loose your soul but hey you can shape change.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T19:40:05-07:00","id":1093501,"title":"","content":"Well first, you're going to want to go Dreamspeaker, as the animistic worldview gels very well with a Fera's. Getting the Totem background helps too; a Kinfolk unable to undergo First Change will try to gain the patronage of their tribe's Totem, if at all possible. Doing so would go a long way towards garnering the character respect among their shapechanging relatives.<br /> <br /> Spirit is going to be your primary Sphere, followed by Life obviously. The character will want to shoot for Spirit 4, so they can start creating Fetishes. But you know all that already. To get around the need for Spheres, you'll rely primarily on pacts and deals you can make with spirits.<br /> <br /> Getting a tattoo Wonder that can allow one to shapeshift into an animal is useful, but you'll need to ask someone to make it for you. If you get it as an Artifact, rather than a Talisman, you don't need to ask them to invest one of their precious permanent Willpower dots into the creation (which is a tall ask for anyone). Nonetheless, making an Artifact is a big deal, so whoever makes it for the character will need to be compensated greatly. Because tattoo-focused Wonder creators are specialists, I might suggest that this Wonder be obtained during play, as a part of the plot. The character seeking out someone who can be convinced to do this, and paying the price. If you can't be bothered with that, you can have the character buy it as a background at character creation. But I would suggest a Flaw be taken to compensate for it (and you'll already be investing background dots in Totem), like Debts, or even Enemy. Something to indicate that your character was so intent on being able to change like a true shifter, they bit off more than they could chew. Either incurring a debt they still need to pay, or ducking out before payment was rendered, making enemies in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T20:01:54-07:00","id":1093508,"title":"","content":"Next, you'll want to consider what <i>kind</i> of Kinfolk you are. Which tribe is your character most closely related to? Because that obviously shapes your character's Backgrounds, Abilities, and specific outlook. A Wendigo kinfolk will draw more of their Practices from Native American medicine work, while a Get of Fenris will draw more heavily from Norse practices. A Bone Gnawer will likely be a transient (low or no Resources, but perhaps lots of Survival and street Contacts), and be drawn more towards being an Urban Shaman. Similarly, a Glass Walker kinfolk will gravitate towards Technoshamanism - working with spirits of technology and the Weaver - while having dots in Technology, Computer, and Drive. Stargazer kinfolk, by contrast, are more likely to join the Akashayana, particularly the shamanistic Jnani; they'll pursue Mind arts as well as Spirit, in the interests of mastering Astral Projection.<br /> <br /> A Bestet kinfolk who Awakens may have a distinct advantage in all tribes save Swara: they can learn to step sideways. Combined with the breed's reputation as sorcerers and tricksters, and a magic-using Bastet kinfolk could become prized among its shifter cousins. A Kitsune kinfolk, however, is likely to be envied by their relatives if they Awaken. After all, they have access to a form of magic that a True Kitsune never will; if a Kitsune is willing to capture a Mage and try to torture the secrets of True Magick from them (as they've been known to do), what do you think they'll do to their kinfolk for &quot;holding out on them&quot;? A Nagah kinfolk, because of their breed's duty, may find themselves most at home among the Euthanatos, delivering death to those that need to die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 05-16-2017, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T20:51:08-07:00","id":1093523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zulkir Jhor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1093459-how-to-cheat-at-being-a-shapechanger#post1093459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, I am not looking for something overpowered or broken.<br /> <br /> For a game, one player was talking about making an Kinfolk that was unhappy that they didn't change. After the character Awoke they have been trying to use magic, wonders and anything else they can find to gain what they feel is their rightful abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does he consider his &quot;rightful&quot; abilities? I mean other people are going to tell you how you need to be super nice to Totems and all that shit but the simple truth is as hard as the character tries He is spitting in the face of Gaia's intentions.. of course that's what mages do.<br /> <br /> So what does he want? the power to take the form of beasts? to command the spirits?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While I know the easy answers of use Sphere X to do effect X, I am wondering if anyone has unique or interesting ideas for a mage to cheat at being a shapechanger of any kind. We are not looking to recreate Samuel Haight or get the full powers of being a were-whatever, but to find thematically interesting ways to move forward with this idea.<br /> <br /> Especially beneficial is any way of accomplishing any particular feat without the player needing Spheres; for example Forged by Dragons Fire has a wonder tattoo that allows one to shapechange into one particular animal and certain fetishes from Werewolf could help. </div> </div> </div>Wonders are just magical effects in a physical form. Broadly speaking to get a tattoo that lets you turn into an animal you need someone who can turn into an animal and has Prime 5 I think. He could also theoretically get a fetish with the power bound into it(the traditional wolf belt for example). As Mage he has access to Spirits generally not interacted with regularly by Fera.<br /> <br /> So the option I'd see for him are:Have an Older mage who's down with his stuff who has the toys to give him the fetish or wonder. This still leads to him having to get the right ingredients and tass. Start with a Wonder or Blessing or Device that just lets him shapeshift. Nothing keeps him from having hunted down the appropriate WOnder or Wondermaker or Devicer or Blesser before start of game(conversely you know hunt down a person who can do it, Or start with a Mentor who can who will send you on your way to it)<br /> <br /> There is also Spirit Pacting, which gets into &quot;Summon and appropriate spirit, offer it an apporpirate bribe.&quot; but essentially this is another method of &quot;get Wonder/Blessing/etc&quot;<br /> <br /> He could take a totem and spend extra points to have it grant him shapeshifting. IT could be a power granted by a Familiar or Spirit Ally.<br /> <br /> Or he could pick up a Pooka buddy with Metamorphosis as the Art who'll change you when its cool. <br /> <br /> He could steal a treasure from the Fairies who have said power in it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T03:20:20-07:00","id":1093599,"title":"","content":"Here's a terrible alternative idea. Have them go Marauder and believe they are already a shapeshifter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T15:41:00-07:00","id":1093871,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the help. It is really appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8764-zulkir-jhor","name":"Zulkir Jhor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}